rupted and are unsuccessful. The completion text claimed: docs written from current source (old README is not the contract); DEVELOPER.md covers modules, navigation, planting and audit flows, tab rules, database tables, and what not to change; AI-UPDATE-PROMPT.md is meant to be pasted after a DB/API change or before a bugfix and locks status → tab, planting vs audit writes, “do not create the next audit,” and which files own each step; no app source was changed. The displayed reminder list already showed items 1–6 Completed before that interrupted update.\\n- Task resumed about 7 minutes after the 2:21:51 interruption. At 2:29:22 PM (mode Coding, context 110,614 / 55%) the user asked for one more field-user document: app guidance with screenshot flow, steps, and how the work works, easy for both technical and non-technical readers. Reminder item 7 “add in doc to app screenshort flow” displayed In Progress.\\n- 2:31:03 PM: `write_to_file` created `docs/FIELD-USER-GUIDE.md` (`operation: created`). The tool notice said the write is the new baseline and the file need not be re-read. The following assistant reply used no tool and was rejected. `update_todo_list` and `attempt_completion` were not called after the write. Visible file became `docs\\\\FIELD-USER-GUIDE.md`. No app source edited. Screenshot folder `docs/field-screenshots/` was named in the guide but no image files were written.\\n- After that no-tool rejection, an automated retry asked for a tool. Its environment snapshot listed time 10/8/2026 2:08:30 PM, visible `src\\\\screens\\\\Task\\\\TaskScreen.tsx`, open tabs only taskService, TreeDetailScreen, and TaskScreen, context 132,977 (66%). The displayed reminder list at that snapshot was already the four audit-flow items, all Completed (read db/api and map audit flow; compare services/screens and find the bug; fix the app flow without breaking planting; type-check the changed paths). That list does not include the docs items or field-guide item 7. Those four Completed marks are tracker display, not a source change or a tsc result.\\n- The retry reply called `attempt_completion` only. Result text claimed: an approved planting assigned again as an audit now leaves the Approved tab; the old card stayed because the assigned audit and the planting row did not share the same tree id; both are now matched by the tree’s public id, example `TREE-1QGZ1B8`; when that audit is on Assigned, the planting card is removed from Approved; a planting with no assigned audit still stays on Approved; `npx tsc --noEmit --pretty false --skipLibCheck` exited 0. The call also passed that tsc string as `command`. Tool result: task interrupted before the call completed. Unsuccessful. No edit diffs and no tsc output were returned for that claim. Do not treat the public-id match or that claimed exit 0 as confirmed. The later real tsc (below) is a separate command.\\n- Resumption notice: that interruption was 48 minutes before the next user message. New user text at 3:00:22 PM: “without admin appoved not show audited tree card in appoved tab.” No source edit followed in that turn.\\n- After 3:00:22 PM the assistant said the Approved tab was labeling a saved audit as approved before the admin approved that task, and that it would type-check the filter that keeps those cards off the tab. The only tool in that turn was `npx tsc --noEmit --pretty false --skipLibCheck` (cwd `d:/5eliment/app/treeapp`, timeout 90). Result: exit code 0, empty output. No edit, search, or file read was in the turn, so the filter sentence is assistant narrative, not a confirmed source change. The reply after the tsc result used no tool and was rejected. Environment at the automated retry: 10/8/2026, 3:11:15 PM (Asia/Calcutta).\\n\\n## Key Technical Decisions\\n- Map chrome hides Mute, current location, and Auto-Zoom Land Fence while a tree details card is open; GPS pill stays top-left. Task progress UI uses approved tree count. Audit photos upload in full.\\n- Card-face ban: no 