d tree with an open assigned/in_progress audit task is no longer `isApproved`. Unchanged flags:\\n  ```\\n  const hasAudits = audits.length > 0;\\n  const showAuditProfile = hasAudits || Boolean(asAuditProfile);\\n  const rejectedAuditRound =\\n    isRejected &&\\n    (task?.task_type === 'audit' ||\\n      Number(task?.audit_round) > 0 ||\\n      (showAuditProfile && task?.task_type !== 'capture'))\\n      ? Number(task?.audit_round) || Number(latestAudit?.monitoring_round) || 1\\n      : 0;\\n  const isRejectedAudit = rejectedAuditRound > 0;\\n  const canStartAudit =\\n    Boolean(showSaveAudit) &&\\n    (task?.status === 'assigned' || task?.status === 'in_progress') &&\\n    (task?.task_type === 'audit' || Number(task?.audit_round) > 0);\\n  const hasBottomAction =\\n    (!showAuditProfile && ((!isApproved && isRejected) || (isApproved && canStartAudit))) ||\\n    (showAuditProfile && (auditStatus.allCompleted || isRejectedAudit || canStartAudit));\\n  const bottomPad = insets.bottom + (hasBottomAction ? 64 : 12);\\n  ```\\n  `asAuditProfile` alone does not start an audit. `showSaveAudit` alone does not either. Because `isApproved` now excludes `isOpenAssignedAudit`, the `isApproved && canStartAudit` arm is false for that open audit.\\n- 5:39 header pill, inserted before the rejected branch. Surrounding JSX outside the replacement was not returned:\\n  ```\\n  ) : isOpenAssignedAudit ? (\\n    <View style={styles.pendingPill}>\\n      <Ionicons name=\\\"clipboard\\\" size={12} color=\\\"#fff\\\" />\\n      <Text style={styles.pendingPillText}>ASSIGNED</Text>\\n    </View>\\n  ) : isRejected ? (\\n  ```\\n  Status pill, not a Save Audit button. `pendingPill` / `pendingPillText` were not defined in the patch. The 6:00 request is about the card’s right-side badge, not this pill. Confirmed 6:02 edits key off `task.status === 'assigned'`, not rendered badge text. Unconfirmed 6:03 edits would key off assigned or in_progress.\\n- TreeDetail linked-task pick, 5:37 read of lines 207–236, not edited later:\\n  ```\\n  const isAuditRow = (row: any) =>\\n    row?.task_type === 'audit' || Number(row?.audit_round) > 0;\\n  const isOpen = (row: any) =>\\n    row?.status === 'assigned' || row?.status === 'in_progress';\\n  const rejectedAuditTask = taskRows\\n    .filter((row) => row?.status === 'rejected' && isAuditRow(row))\\n    .sort((a, b) => Number(b?.audit_round || 0) - Number(a?.audit_round || 0))[0];\\n  const openAuditTask = taskRows\\n    .filter((row) => isOpen(row) && isAuditRow(row))\\n    .sort((a, b) => Number(b?.audit_round || 0) - Number(a?.audit_round || 0))[0];\\n  const requestedTask = taskId\\n    ? taskRows.find((row) => row?.id === taskId)\\n    : null;\\n  const linkedTask =\\n    (showSaveAudit ? requestedTask || openAuditTask : null) ||\\n    (asAuditProfile ? requestedTask || openAuditTask || rejectedAuditTask : null) ||\\n    rejectedAuditTask ||\\n    openAuditTask ||\\n    taskRows.find((row) => row?.status === 'rejected') ||\\n    taskRows.find((row) => row?.id === data.id) ||\\n    taskRows[0];\\n  if (linkedTask) setTask(linkedTask);\\n  ```\\n  Source comment: “The Assigned card names its open audit. That row wins, so a rejected audit of the same tree cannot turn Save Audit into Edit Audit.” That holds only when `showSaveAudit` is true and `requestedTask || openAuditTask` is truthy. If the opened card passes its own `taskId` and that row is the rejected audit, `requestedTask` wins the first clause. If `showSaveAudit` is true but both are missing, the chain can still land on `rejectedAuditTask`. Highest `audit_round` wins inside each filtered list.\\n- Circular import: treeService no longer imports `completeTask`. Baseline task close is the local 4-attempt loop. `completeTask` remains the capture-submit path and the audit-close path. taskService ~394 sets `event_type = 'audit'` and `audit_round` on a task update when the audit option is set; that is not the tree-record insert.\\n- Next-audit creation: 5:35